### Feedback progress and deduplication

Recover the latest **PR feedback checkpoint** for this repository + PR from
this conversation's history and child reports. Record per comment ID + updatedAt
(or a body fingerprint if the API has no edit timestamp), source kind, thread
ID if any, decision, reply ID/URL, applied commit, and any pending question.
Use IDs and versions actually assessed, not a child conversation's updatedAt
or the original thread creation time. Retain earlier objections and author
reaffirmations so a fresh child does not restart an already-settled debate.
Never put secrets or full sensitive comment bodies in the checkpoint.

Build PENDING_FEEDBACK_JSON from FEEDBACK_JSON: new/edited items needing
assessment and unfinished actionable requests, each with its full discussion
context. Include general PR comments and review summaries even when there are
zero unresolved threads. Revisit unchanged items only for relevant new
evidence, a changed head affecting the finding, or a newly satisfied blocker.
Already-published, superseded, or substantively declined items are not fresh
work. A local fix is **pending-push**, not completed: retry its validation/push
even if no new comments arrived. Mark code-change requests handled only after
verifying the fix on the remote PR head (including equivalent rebased commits).
Awaiting-author items stay pending but do not cause repeated replies,
notifications, or spawns while the question and evidence remain unchanged.
Do not discard a thread solely because isOutdated is true; assess whether the
request still applies. Skip satisfied/resolved discussions, but inspect any
new author request added after prior handling, even in a resolved thread.

Triage or delegation alone does not mark a request completed. Record queued
work as queued and mark it handled only after an actual outcome/report.
Before a new spawn, look for the same PR/task child: never race a running
worker; on a later run, give new/edited feedback to the existing idle child.
Spawn only if none exists. Carry the checkpoint and policy into every handoff.
After work, persist an updated compact checkpoint in this conversation's
report (and return it to the parent when delegated), without posting bookkeeping
noise to GitHub. Emit checkpoint updates only when decisions change; on no-op
scheduled runs rely on the existing history/report and remain quiet. Pending
material concerns remain visible as merge blockers.